BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(observation are important. If any sign or symptom of polio is) Tj T*
(present, the affected person should be hospitalized immediately.) Tj T*
(Hospitals have many special forms of equipment which are necessary in) Tj T*
(treatment. Trained nursing care is essential. Should paralysis appear,) Tj T*
(special measures are necessary to prevent or lessen deformity and to) Tj T*
(begin the rebuilding of the affected parts of the body. No clearly) Tj T*
(reliable specific drug is available as yet which will cure polio, but) Tj T*
(gamma globulin appears to give some degree of protection for several) Tj T*
(weeks against the paralysis stage of the disease. There are now strong) Tj T*
(hopes that a vaccine is now available that will give immunity against) Tj T*
(polio for a whole season.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_At the present time_ treatment of the disease takes many forms.) Tj T*
(While a patient is recovering from a polio attack, a full nourishing) Tj T*
(diet, application of various forms of heat and massage, special baths) Tj T*
(and exercises, are the measures which are most helpful in restoring) Tj T*
(usefulness to affected arms or legs. Specially built shoes or braces) Tj T*
(are required in only a few cases, and surgical operations have been) Tj T*
(devised to return motion and function to the arms or legs of some) Tj T*
(patients.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Treatment_ must be continued over long periods of time in some cases,) Tj T*
(but the results are often very rewarding. The expense of such long) Tj T*
(treatment is great. Fortunately, an awakened public, through its) Tj T*
(contributions to the National Foundation for Infantile Paralysis and) Tj T*
(other Agencies, has helped thousands to bear this expense. Support of) Tj T*
(these organizations in their sincere and unselfish aims is a splendid) Tj T*
(public service in the battle against polio.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                _How to GUARD against this DISEASE...._) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Although there is no known means of vaccination or inoculation against) Tj T*
(polio, many things can be done to lessen the possibility of getting the) Tj T*
(disease.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_First_ of all, if an epidemic occurs, you should follow the) Tj T*
(instructions of the local public health officer. He will also decide in) Tj T*
(what cases gamma globulin is needed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Secondly_, it is wise to avoid crowded places, especially indoors) Tj T*
(where there is opportunity for close contact and possible infection.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_In addition_, food and water should be obtained only from absolutely) Tj T*
(reliable sources.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Every_ effort should be made to insure that flies, mice, rats, and) Tj T*
(other vermin are kept out of the home, as they are possible carriers of) Tj T*
(infection.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
