(_You_ and your children should get plenty of rest and wholesome food,) Tj T*
(avoid over-exertion and excessive fatigue.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Do not_ travel into areas where there is much polio or go swimming) Tj T*
(when many cases have occurred in your locality.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Further_, many physicians may advise postponing the removal of) Tj T*
(tonsils, the extraction of teeth, or other operations in or about the) Tj T*
(nose, throat, or mouth when the disease is prevalent in the community.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The National Foundation for Infantile Paralysis and other Agencies will) Tj T*
(help polio patients as much as possible. But the best kind of help) Tj T*
(is that which you, yourself, can give by taking every precaution to) Tj T*
(keep the disease from striking anyone in your family. Proper rest, a) Tj T*
(balanced diet, and moderate exercise in the fresh air and sunshine tone) Tj T*
(up the body and help increase the system?s resistance to disease. By) Tj T*
(following these and other common-sense rules of wholesome living, your) Tj T*
(family will be taking a major step toward health and happiness.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
